---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Checker from '../../../components/Checker.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CAD Compatibility Checker"
  description="Upload a STEP, IGES, or BREP file and get a health report: unit consistency, open shells, non-manifold edges, face orientation, and assembly structure. Nothing is uploaded."
>
  <article class="tool-page wrap">
    <h1>CAD Compatibility Checker</h1>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      Upload a STEP, IGES, or BREP file to check for common problems before
      it causes trouble downstream: inconsistent units, open (non-watertight)
      shells, non-manifold edges, inconsistent face orientation, and
      degenerate geometry in the tessellation — plus a summary of the
      file's assembly structure.
    </p>

    <Checker />

    <div class="notice">
      This tool checks what a browser-based mesh importer can see: unit
      declarations, edge/face manifoldness, orientation consistency, and
      tessellation quality. It does not have access to full CAD-kernel
      B-Rep topology (surface/curve types, true geometric tolerance
      analysis) — it's a fast first pass, not a substitute for opening the
      file in your CAD system.
    </div>

    <p class="tool-footnote">
      Every check runs locally in your browser — nothing you upload here is
      sent anywhere. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page for
      details, and our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for what this tool is
      (and isn't) a substitute for. Related guide:
      <a href="/guides/non-manifold-geometry-step-files/">Why STEP Files Come In Non-Manifold (and How to Fix It)</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
